before:
For normal author declarations, a later layer has higher precedence.
```css
@layer reset, theme;
@layer reset { #message { color: purple; } }
@layer theme { p { color: teal; } }
```
The theme rule wins for the matching paragraph despite the earlier rule’s ID selector.

after:
The first line puts `theme` after `base`. The theme color wins even though the base rule uses an ID selector.
```css
@layer base, theme;
@layer base {
  #message { color: purple; }
}
@layer theme {
  p { color: teal; }
}
```
Both selectors match the supplied paragraph.
